.TH shiftpaper-bake 1  shiftpaper 
.SH NAME
shiftpaper\-bake \- Bake an image without setting it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshiftpaper bake\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bake an image without setting it.
.PP
Runs the depth model on the image and writes a colour PNG and a 16\-bit depth PNG, `<hash>.color.png` and `<hash>.depth16.png`, to the cache or to \-\-out, then prints their paths. Baking the same image again reuses them. `set` and `slideshow` bake for you, so you only need this for an image you\*(Aqll put in config.toml yourself, like one for a single monitor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Where to write the files. Defaults to the cache, ~/.cache/shiftpaper/wallpapers
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
The ONNX depth model to bake with. Defaults to $SHIFTPAPER_MODEL, then the one in config.toml
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Source image (jpeg, png, or webp)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
shiftpaper bake photo.jpg                 Bake into the cache
shiftpaper bake photo.jpg \-\-out ~/walls   Bake into a folder of your own
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
shiftpaper(1)
.PP
The docs: https://github.com/CPritch/shiftpaper/tree/main/docs
